<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/01e66e34845e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-Driving Bus Crashes Two Hours After Being Put on the Road" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "231" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/02628afaa057> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Within its first hours of operation Wednesday, an autonomous shuttle bus that is part of a ballyhooed study of driverless vehicles on public roads in Las Vegas was involved in a collision with a truck." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "229" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/07021515d272> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It took less than two hours for Las Vegas’s brand new self-driving shuttle to end up in a crash on Wednesday—thanks to a human." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/092c640655e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A driverless shuttle bus being tested in Las Vegas was involved in a crash an hour into its first day on the job - although it wasn't the vehicle's fault." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "222" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e6c66c6e5ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Digital Trends was onboard the ill-fated Las Vegas self-driving shuttle" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "234" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/12668866e076> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle is part of a one-year pilot project, sponsored by the American Automobile Association of Northern California, Nevada and Utah." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "230" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/127adc33393d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A self-driving shuttle was launched in Las Vegas to great celebration and acclaim." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "231" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/132b57ab6cd5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "There have been 12 crashes in California alone since Sept. 8 involving General Motors Co’s self-driving unit, Cruise Automation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "238" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/134ec8eb885c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Las Vegas' self-driving bus crashes in first hour of service" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "226" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/147676e11d51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Even so, the National Transportation Safety Board, the federal agency that investigates major crashes and issues safety recommendations, dispatched investigators to review what happened in Las Vegas." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1765ddcb1f0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Driverless bus in crash after two hours on road in Las Vegas" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "223" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1a132a238a3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Automobile Association of America (AAA) of Southern Nevada, one of the shuttle’s sponsors, said it would assist the safety board’s investigation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/239cbff98c95> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for AAA, which is working with Las Vegas and Keolis to sponsor the program and survey driver attitudes toward autonomous vehicles, confirmed on Twitter that the accident was actually the truck driver’s fault." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "235" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/264fb6558cc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Las Vegas Won't Stop Driverless Shuttle Program after Fatal Accident in Arizona" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "225" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a3b46132ff1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Uber vehicle was in autonomous mode with an operator behind the wheel when it hit the woman, who was walking outside of a crosswalk, Tempe, Ariz., police said today." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "225" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2c10b22e89bb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some press reports are quoting a statement released by the City of Las Vegas, suggesting the collision could have been prevented if the truck had been equipped with the same collision avoidance technology the bus was using." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "230" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/34f5f53e7746> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Save this picture! Image via screenshot from video © Keolis Commuter Services" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "219" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37aeb5de531b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[235] The shuttle, made by French startup Navya and owned and operated by French private transportation company Keolis, operates on a 0.6-mile loop around downtown Las Vegas offering free rides to residents." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "235" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/384608c8ca82> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Car & Driver, which put together a super-detailed report on the accident, spoke to a Keolis rep said the shuttle worked as intended." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e0e3b5557e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Las Vegas self-driving bus crashed into on its first day" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "218" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3ed9d7eccbef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[217] Las Vegas police officer Aden Ocampo-Gomez said the truck's driver was at fault for the crash and was cited for illegal backing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "217" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3f998dd2d8c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "City spokesman Jace Radke said the shuttle stopped when it sensed the lorry was approaching, but the larger vehicle kept moving." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "223" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41c7416d56c8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving bus involved in accident on its first day" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "237" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42b654077ab5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving bus involved in crash less than two hours after Las Vegas launch" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4b8b4c5dd7a5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The shuttle did what it was supposed to do, in that its sensors registered the truck and the shuttle stopped,” the city said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4ba0b0a0c3cc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle did what it was supposed to do, in that its sensors registered the truck and the shuttle stopped to avoid the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "219" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5275e1179844> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving bus gets into accident on its first day in Las Vegas, human driver blamed for collision" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "220" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d4c32059f3e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“If only the truck had the autonomous technology, this would likely not have occurred.” Moreno said responding officers issued a citation to the driver of the truck." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "229" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6afd03e22bb9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "No injuries were reported and, within a day, the shuttle—operated by transit company Keolis and built by French-based Navya ARMA—was back on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6be1063579f4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-Driving Bus in Las Vegas Crashes Just 2 Hours After Launch" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "219" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c768c8840aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The NAVYA shuttle comes equipped with LiDAR technology, GPS, cameras, and will seat eight passengers with seatbelts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "233" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/76016445c538> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[234] My suggestion to Navya and Keolis is that if the shuttle doesn't have cameras and LIDAR facing backwards, it would be good to enable the shuttle to reverse if something's coming toward it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "234" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/763deb516892> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Various media outlets are reporting a fender bender collision (literally) between a driverless shuttle bus and a tractor-trailer in Las Vegas on Nov. 8." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "230" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7837be167603> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "City spokesman Jace Radke said the shuttle took two more loops after the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/793070c7e94e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Federal transportation safety officials headed to Las Vegas on Friday to investigate a collision this week between a self-driving shuttle bus on its first day of service and a truck, which was blamed on human error." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/79cb5416816e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Truck Driver Gets the Blame in Driverless Shuttle Bus Crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "230" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a472e777c99> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[232] The Navya Arma, an autonomous and electric vehicle operated by Keolis North America, went into service on Wednesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7dc760fdf9d5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber has been testing the self-driving vehicles in Tempe and Phoenix for months." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "225" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7e15c7437ba7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for AAA, which is sponsoring the latest pilot program, said on Twitter that the accident was due to \"human error\" on the part of the truck driver." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "226" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/84b7dbf0d6e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Horseless carriages are now driverless in in Phoenix, thanks to Waymo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "234" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c8442b1ef3c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-Driving-Shuttle Era Begins with a First-Day Crash in Vegas" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "229" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8db36a3e3018> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle did what it was supposed to do, in that its sensors registered the truck and the shuttle stopped to avoid the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "220" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8de2c2d4e6dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A self-driving shuttle in Las Vegas got into an accident on its first day of service" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "235" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/96de838bf4c9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The bus, a 12-seat Navya Arma, was on the first day a 12-month trial covering a 0.6-mile (1-kilometer) loop in Las Vegas' Fremont East “Innovation District” when it was grazed by a reversing truck." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "219" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9719be4656bb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Beyond its autonomous capabilities, Keolis said the shuttle is the first autonomous vehicle to integrate with traffic lights, which could lead to improved traffic flow and reduced congestion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "229" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9979751a55e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving shuttle bus crashes on first day of testing" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "228" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c7655d3bde1> a airo:Evidence ;
