<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a21c85102ca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "There have been 12 crashes in California alone since September 8 involving General Motors self-driving unit, Cruise Automation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/38bc461f602a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It uses GPS and electronic kerb sensors to navigate the roads." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "223" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/69449f158252> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The autonomous shuttle was testing today when it was grazed by a delivery truck downtown." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "236" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a0d2675ee1ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for AAA, which is a sponsor of the planned yearlong study, said the shuttle stopped as it sensed the truck ahead and remained stationary when the truck backed into the left-front side of the shuttle, which carried multiple passengers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "229" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ad04645f4b9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In September, the board produced an extensive review of a fatal 2016 crash involving a Tesla owner whose car was operating in its semi-autonomous Autopilot mode—so it’s not surprising to see it taking interest in the minor bump involving a driverless shuttle, even if the shuttle wasn’t at fault." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/afb0ecdc996b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An incident involving a Tesla Model S, which has some autonomous functions, killed a man in 2016." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2188" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4469768d729> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AAA in partnership with Keolis, launched the largest self-driving shuttle pilot project in the United States to operate in live traffic on 8 November." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "233" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1de42176772d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The U.S. transportation department and lawmakers have so far taken a relatively hands-off approach to testing of autonomous vehicles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4da7cce063c0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Jenny Wong, 1 of the eight people on board, told KSNV." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "236" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6266c2838db7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier this year an autonomous vehicle being tested by ride-sharing company Uber in Arizona rolled over after another driver on the road failed to give way." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2188" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/78fe77f77fd4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[Keolis rep Chris] Barker said the attendant can use the controller to guide the shuttle through thorny situations, such as if a traffic light is out and a police officer is guiding traffic through an intersection." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/89c8c6dd7f78> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chris Barker, spokesman for the shuttle operator, Keolis North America, says the bus performed the way it was designed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "230" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9328cb6d8353> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The self-driving shuttle pilot project in downtown Las Vegas, which began in November, is a joint venture by AAA, the transportation company Keolis and the city." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "225" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98cc127b5efa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Las Vegas police officer Aden Ocampo-Gomez said the truck’s driver was at fault for the crash and was cited for illegal backing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d689cb32a000> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The project is a collaboration between the American Automobile Association, transportation firm Kelois and tech firm Navya." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "236" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ed3e8a6667a3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Jenny Wong, a passenger on the shuttle at the time of the crash, told local news station KSNV: “The shuttle just stayed still." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7eddede1fa6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The NTSB investigated a May 2016 crash of a Tesla Inc Model S that killed a driver using the vehicle’s semi-autonomous “Autopilot” system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "238" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3dfda46ef2d8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Navya also says that its buses are equipped with the latest Lidar, stereo camera and GPS technology to ensure that they are safe on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "228" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a63404c76a9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle is also sponsored by the city of Las Vegas, Keolis North America and the Regional Transportation Commission of Southern Nevada." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5e210bd48bbe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Almost all the incidents recorded by Waymo, Google's autonomous vehicle arm, have been down to human drivers hitting the vehicles, and a major crash involving Uber's driverless cars in March was down to the driver of the other car." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "222" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5e9202511ffc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle is also sponsored by the city of Las Vegas, Keolis North America and the Regional Transportation Commission of Southern Nevada." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "238" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6eebd181eb74> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The NTSB investigated a May 2016 crash of a Tesla Model S that killed a driver using the vehicle’s semi-autonomous “Autopilot” system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/91ac2b89cfc7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The collision comes a day after Waymo - owned by Google's parent company Alphabet - announced it is launching a fully self-driving fleet of taxis in Phoenix, Arizona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2188" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a91a4c627fee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Navya Arma, an autonomous and electric vehicle operated by Keolis North America, went into service on Wednesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "232" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d47bd7206e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After a pedestrian was hit and killed Sunday by an Uber self-driving car in Arizona, the city of Las Vegas said it has no plans to take its driverless shuttle off the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "225" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bcea8c72d550> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Jeff Zurschmeide, a writer for Digital Trends who was on board at the time, said he did not hear the horn." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "224" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f43849ad1f03> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Built by French company Navya, the bus was carrying eight passengers when it collided with a truck." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "218" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/212ada741b14> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shuttle is the first of its kind in the US, and Navya, the French tech firm behind the bus, is also performing test programmes in London and Paris." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "228" .

