<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2ec05742f389> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Developed by French company Navya, it uses GPS, electronic kerb sensors and other technology to find its way at no more than 15mph." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "217" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b4a4893a0050> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Before it crashed, dozens of people had lined up to get a free trip on a 0.6-mile loop around Fremont East, Las Vegas, including Nascar driver Danica Patrick and magic duo Penn and Teller." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "227" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/435f8ce3e54a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google sibling Waymo announced on Tuesday that it is launching a fully autonomous Uber-like ride-hailing service with no human driver behind the wheel in Phoenix, Arizona in the next few months." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "217" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d60711288519> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waymo still plans to move forward with launching a ride-hailing service featuring autonomous vehicles in Phoenix, Arizona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "231" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f2671b22eab5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier the same day, Google sibling Waymo announced it had begun operating its driverless cars on the streets of Phoenix, Arizona with no human behind the wheel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "218" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5c8f2460157> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It’s a joint project put together by the City of Las Vegas, AAA, the Regional Transportation Commission of Southern Nevada, and the Keolis North America company, which runs mass transit in Las Vegas." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "234" .

